WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:03.124
- [Narrator] Deep inside
the Greco-Roman City

00:00:03.124 --> 00:00:05.824
of Hierapolis lies the most relaxing

00:00:05.824 --> 00:00:09.661
and the most visited
site in all of Turkey.

00:00:09.661 --> 00:00:13.131
(lively, bouncy music)

00:00:13.131 --> 00:00:16.219
From a distance, Pamukkale's
cascading white pools

00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:19.469
seem to resemble a
castle of fluffy cotton,

00:00:19.469 --> 00:00:21.899
but upon closer inspection,
they reveal themselves

00:00:21.899 --> 00:00:24.459
to be solid limestone
walls housing turquoise,

00:00:24.459 --> 00:00:26.042
mineral-rich water.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.522
The site is fittingly called Pamukkale,

00:00:29.522 --> 00:00:34.051
which translates to
Cotton Castle in Turkish.

00:00:34.051 --> 00:00:36.963
Housing 17 hot springs, they
each range in temperature

00:00:36.963 --> 00:00:41.130
from 35 degrees to 100 degrees,
perfect for soaking in.

00:00:42.531 --> 00:00:45.072
Pamukkale has been used
as a natural bathing spot

00:00:45.072 --> 00:00:47.190
for centuries, especially since the water

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:50.559
in each hot spring is
filled with minerals.

00:00:50.559 --> 00:00:52.192
It was the Greek and Romans who discovered

00:00:52.192 --> 00:00:53.869
that these minerals potentially hold

00:00:53.869 --> 00:00:56.280
countless curative properties.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.651
According to many, the
water brings benefits

00:00:58.651 --> 00:01:01.381
to the skin, eyes, and
can assist with recovery

00:01:01.381 --> 00:01:04.421
from high blood pressure,
making this Cotton Castle

00:01:04.421 --> 00:01:07.004
a very relaxing place to visit.

00:01:12.969 --> 00:01:15.136
(chiming)

